-- MEMBERS ON A TYPE ALIAS ---------------------------------------- src/Main.fic

I am parsing a type alias, but I got stuck at this `where`:

4| type alias Meters =
5|     Float
6|     where
       ^
A type alias is only another name for an existing type, so it cannot carry
members of its own. Two names for one type would have to share one set of
members.

If you want a type with its own functions, wrap the type in a custom type:

    type Meters = Meters Float
        where
            add : Meters -> Meters -> Meters
            add (Meters a) (Meters b) = Meters (a + b)
